# Apixaban + 10 Acetonitrile: XTB2 MD, spherical confinement
# Analogous to the other Apixaban Explicit10 confined XTB2 MD runs
# (Apixaban/Water/MD, Apixaban/DMSO/MD/10, Apixaban/MeOH/MD/10,
#  Apixaban/Chloroform/MD/10, Apixaban/DMF/MD, Apixaban/Acetone/MD).
#
# Starting geometry: Apixaban (59 atoms) using the REAL r2SCAN-3c/
#   SMD(acetonitrile)-optimized geometry
#   (Apixaban_SMD_acetonitrile_Opt_Freq_KeepDens.xyz, converged,
#   E = -1542.153770 Eh). 10 Acetonitrile molecules use the REAL
#   r2SCAN-3c/SMD(acetonitrile)-optimized monomer geometry
#   (Acetonitrile/r2SCAN3c/Monomer_r2SCAN3c_SMD.xyz, converged,
#   E = -132.727236 Eh), each placed with its N atom (the primary H-bond
#   acceptor / most polar site) on the same 12-direction sphere-shell
#   pattern used throughout this project, rotated so the molecule's bulk
#   (the C#C-CH3 chain) points radially outward.
#
# Apixaban centroid = (31.537, -19.865, -0.109); max atom-centroid distance
#   = 9.02 Ang (consistent with the other Apixaban Explicit10 builds).
# Acetonitrile's own extent from its N reference atom = 3.14 Ang.
# 10 Acetonitrile molecules placed at offset 12.78 Ang from Apixaban's
#   centroid (the standard offset used throughout this project).
# Cell Sphere radius set to 16.0 Ang.
# Checked: min Acetonitrile-Apixaban atom distance = 4.17 Ang (no clash),
#   max atom distance from the sphere center = 15.78 Ang (safely inside the
#   16.0 Ang sphere). Total atom count = 119 (59 + 10x6), verified.

! XTB2 MD

%md
  Timestep 1.0_fs
  Initvel 298.15_K
  Thermostat NHC 298.15_K Timecon 20.0_fs
  Cell Sphere 31.537, -19.865, -0.109, 16.0 Spring 20
  Dump Position Stride 100 Filename "Apixaban_10MeCN_XTB_preequil_confined.xyz"
  Run 20000
end

